  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantNotesRegardingFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-19" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;1.In accordance with 18 CFR Part 352, the FERC Uniform System of Accounts (USoA) requires that receivables and payables&#8212;including those with affiliated companies&#8212;be reported on a gross basis, ensuring that balances are clearly distinguished and accurately presented in the applicable regulatory schedules. Reporting processes are aligned with this end in mind.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantNotesRegardingFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
